From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:03:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] avoid quadratic accumulation of rectangles in
 box_rep::redraw

The rectangles returned by the children were collected with l= ll * l,
which copies both lists: quadratic (and deeply recursive) in the number
of redrawn children.  Prepend them instead.
---
 src/Typeset/Boxes/Basic/boxes.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Typeset/Boxes/Basic/boxes.cpp b/src/Typeset/Boxes/Basic/boxes.cpp
index fc915bd40..54c46bff6 100644
--- a/src/Typeset/Boxes/Basic/boxes.cpp
+++ b/src/Typeset/Boxes/Basic/boxes.cpp
@@ -564,8 +564,10 @@ box_rep::redraw (renderer ren, path p, rectangles& l) {
       if (!is_nil(ll)) {
         i1= min (i1, k);
         i2= max (i2, k);
-        l = ll * l;
-        ll= rectangles ();
+        // Prepend the new rectangles instead of "l= ll * l": list concatenation
+        // copies both operands (recursively), which made this loop quadratic
+        // (and deeply recursive) in the number of redrawn children.
+        for (; !is_nil (ll); ll= ll->next) l= rectangles (ll->item, l);
       }
     }
     
